  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "round-heads-sahara-s019-p00167",
      "source_en": "Horses are known in the Sahara from the early 3rd millennium BP (Smith 1992), so that the Caballine phase dates from circa 2,800 to 1,500 BP. It overlaps with the subsequent Camel period dated from circa 2,000 BP until recently (Barnett & Mattingly 2003). The two last chronologicalstylistic groups of Caballine and Cameline styles belong to the historical era and will not be considered in the present book.",
